WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Golden Globe
award-winning actor

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from films
such as "Moulin Rouge"

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.806 line:92%
and the "Star Wars" prequels

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well as his work
in the FX series "Fargo."

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.779 size:88% position:44%
He's currently starring
in "Halston" on Netflix.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:13.680 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Halston, these are not bad.
-They're not good.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, this one is.
"Effortless and elegant,

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:25.692
Halston is an exciting new voice
in women's fashion."

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well..."The look
they've assembled here

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
is thrown together
or contrived."

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, which is it,
Bernadine Mars,

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.200 line:92%
thrown together or contrived?"

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.071
-This one says, "'You're eithe
young or old,' says Halston.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's neither
good nor bad.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's just a quote.
He never, ever gets to talk.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:45.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show Ewan McGregor.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hello, Ewan!
-Hey. How are you?

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm doing very well.
It's lovely to see you again

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.085 line:92%
-It's nice to see you, too

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:54.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now I want
to talk about "Halston,"

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I want to talk about
some of your work

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:59.659
that I became familiar wit
over the pandemic that you

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess, have been doing
for a long time,

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is narrating nature
documentaries for BBC Scotland

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:09.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did that come about?
-Yeah.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:09.836 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I can't remember.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:13.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was approached
by the director of them.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um...and I started
doing these narrations.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
And because it's Scotland,
it's so close to --

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.783 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Video glitching ]

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
...I just loved sitting ther
in the recording booth,

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.122
looking at these
beautiful images of my homeland,

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:32.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, and nature and
the wildlife that lives there.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:35.161
And I just fell into doing them.
I've done like four of the

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
or something,
four different series.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:39.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, um...I like it.
I get to be David Attenborough

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.768
but the Scottish version,
you know, for a little bit

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is nice.
-You're very good at it,

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:46.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I do have
a bone to pick with you,

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.174 line:92%
which is, early in the pandemic,

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we were
at our most stressed --

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm stuck at home
with my kids --

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my son
has this book about birds.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.548 size:78% position:39%
He would pick a bird,
and I'd try to find

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
a YouTube video
of one of the birds.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:02:02.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
We find the guillemot,
and I start watching this vide

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
of you narrating it,
and I'm thinking,

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Ewan's not gonna
lead me astray."

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:07.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know --
You remember this?

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the most harrowing vide
I've ever seen.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.832
-It's the most upsetting thing
you'll ever have seen, yeah.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, let's just show
what I'm watching

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:18.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
with my, at the time,
4-year-old son.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:18.771 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
A razorbill
makes a final attack.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:26.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Birds squawking ]

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:27.046 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Gasps ]

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:31.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
Unable to steer, it's headin
straight for the rocks.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ohh!

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.422 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.692
-I mean, that is the worst -
-No, no, but listen, listen.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
But listen.
What happens thereafter

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.798 size:84% position:42%
is there's a shot of it
coming out of the water

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
and climbing back up
on the rock.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I slammed
the laptop shut.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.972 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I didn't see that part.
-There is a shot

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they cut to before
they see it coming back out.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:03:01.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, I know that might be
because it's not the same bird

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.883 size:84% position:42%
coming out of the water
as when we just saw it

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
smashing off the rock, right
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I said to the director,
I said, "You got to promise me

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.123 size:75% position:38%
that's the same bird
'cause I don't think

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:10.823 size:81% position:41% line:92%
that's the same bird."

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:14.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he assures me that
this is what happens in nature

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They fall off.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
So how do they
get down into the water?

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because the parents
try and lure them down.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:21.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're down there, coming
"Come on, son, jump!"

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the birds are quite rightl
going, "[Bleep] that."

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"I'm not doing that."

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:33.746
-Do you remember what the name
of the young birds are called?

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Jumplings.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Excuse me?
-They're literally called

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:40.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
jumplings, according to th
narrator, which is you.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.788 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
Probably making it up
on the fly.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.392
-I know, it's so harrowing
But they're all of them --

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:49.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because there's such drama
in nature,

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.898
and all of the series I've done,
there's these --

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:54.300 size:88% position:44%
You know, I'm in there,
recording it, and often,

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's the first time
I'll have seen it

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
is when I'm actually
recording it.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:04:02.542
There was one with killer whales
and dolphins being --

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, there's one
of a dolphin kind of --

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:07.380
[ Laughing ] It's a huge -
He's got this huge fish,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he can't get it
down his neck.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the fish
is coming out of his mouth

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like a horror film!
It's just horrendous.

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.822 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Anyway, it's fun to do.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:18.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
it's a cruel world out there

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:22.262
-It's a cruel world out there.
It's also was a very cruel world

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:26.199
for all of us this year, and I
read that you did one this year,

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:29.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
another documentary for
the same production company,

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:33.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the sweltering heat
of Los Angeles.

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:37.977 size:84% position:42%
-Yes. It was a series
called "The Stormborn."

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:42.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
Animals that are born
in a storm, like, in Scotlan

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:47.353
and Norway and all of that
bad-weather area up there.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.588 line:92%
And they asked me to do it

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.123 size:84% position:42%
And, of course, then,
we all got locked down.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was in L.A.,
and I couldn't get

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
to Scotland to do it,
and he couldn't come over.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:57.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I just said,
"Look, you know, all of us --"

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like we're doing now,
we had to adapt,

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:00.333 line:92%
and, you know, keep going.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:04.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I got this little sort of
portable setup.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:07.573 size:81% position:41%
I was doing narrations
for some other things.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I was
in post production

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
for our motorbike trip
"Long Way Up"

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:12.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I did it
with my friend Charley.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:17.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I had the microphone setu
and my laptop,

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was able
to sort of patch in

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:22.121
and do this kind of work,
you know, narration stuff,

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.656 size:78% position:39% line:92%
so I did it that way.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I didn't --
I couldn't find --

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was nowhere
that I could --

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I've got kids,
and there was nowhere

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
I could find
that was quiet enough

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
without risk
of someone battering in

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
disturbing the recording.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I had
this tiny little caravan.

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:38.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-And we call it a caravan

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:40.873
where I'm from, and there
was this little caravan

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:41.574 size:81% position:41% line:92%
over up in the corner.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.744
And I managed to get in like
a little Wi-Fi booster in there.

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:46.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just sat in there,
and I started --

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:47.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said to them,
"It's gonna be fine.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've got my setup."
And we started in the morning,

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:55.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
and by about 11:00, I was
absolutely dripping in sweat

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:56.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
I couldn't --
'Cause I couldn't put

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:59.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
my little air conditioner on
because it was too noisy.

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:03.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I ended up in my underpants
just sitting in my caravan

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:07.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
in my pants,
speaking into my microphon

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the little jumplings
You know.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:12.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you're talking abou
Scottish winter storms.

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:15.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Well, that's -- I'm an actor

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:18.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's what we do, Seth.

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:19.112 line:92%
-Everybody said, they're like,

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
"If anybody can do it,
it's Ewan."

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:24.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, this is really cool
to play Halston.

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:29.021
Obviously, this is a very famous
fashion designer,

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:31.057 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and you got some time --

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:32.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or, I should say,
you took some time

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:36.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get to know some people
who knew him firsthand.

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:37.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
I was really lucky.

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:41.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, there are some peopl
in his world,

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:45.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
who kindly sat down with me,
people he worked with.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:49.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
the most amazing friendshi

00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:50.476 line:92%
he had was with Liza Minnelli.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:54.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they had a really beautifu
best friendship.

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:57.984 line:92%
And I wanted to meet her.

00:06:57.984 --> 00:07:00.486 line:92%
I wanted to meet her anywa

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:03.956 size:84% position:42%
and reassure her that
he was in good hands --

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.024 line:92%
he was in safe hands with me

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:08.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
That I wanted her to know
that I respected

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:10.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
their friendship,
and I understood

00:07:10.897 --> 00:07:12.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he was
very important to her.

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:16.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I couldn't have imagined
you know, just how --

00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:17.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
She asked me to keep
our conversation private,

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:21.974
which I would always respect
but I got -- what she gave to me

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
was the great love
she had for him,

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.678 line:92%
and I could see through her,

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:27.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, the great love
he had for her.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:30.550 line:92%
So, it was a really beautiful --

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:33.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, it was very shortl
after I met Liza,

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:35.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went off and started
playing Halston.

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:38.291
It's a responsibility, you know,
when you're playing somebody

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:42.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's lived
and to get him right.

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:44.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was lucky
that she was able

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:46.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
to share some of her memorie
of him with me.

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:50.369
-Yeah, I will say,
insofar as having to do research

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:51.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a part,
you can do a lot worse

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
than having to sit down
with Liza Minnelli.

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:55.675
That seems like as good as
it gets, as far as research.

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:58.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was ama-- it was brilliant
It was brilliant.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was such an honor
to meet her.

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:01.380 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, really.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:05.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is always an honor
to have you here.

00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:07.553 line:92%
I can't wait to see the show

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:11.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we are gonna go out
with a clip of the guillemot

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:13.192 line:92%
crawling out of the water.

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:15.194 size:75% position:38%
And then our viewers
can go back and see

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:16.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
if they think
it's the same bird.

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:20.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
I mean, it's 50/50, isn't it

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:21.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Or maybe even the odds

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:24.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
